{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '370,550p' src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj; cat test/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj | head -55; cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"   (a path relative to `<dir>`) as `auto_prepend_file`, and return the\n   parsed `{:out :diag :uncaught :exit}`.\"\n  [dir file prepend-file]\n  (let [{:keys [out err exit]}\n        (sh/sh \"docker\" \"run\" \"--rm\"\n               \"-v\" (str (.toAbsolutePath (.toPath (io/file dir))) \":/w\")\n               \"-w\" \"/w\"\n               \"php:8.3-cli\" \"php\"\n               \"-d\" \"display_errors=1\"\n               \"-d\" \"html_errors=0\"\n               \"-d\" \"error_reporting=E_ALL\"\n               \"-d\" \"log_errors=0\"\n               \"-d\" (str \"auto_prepend_file=/w/\" prepend-file)\n               file\n               :out-enc \"UTF-8\")]\n    (assoc (parse-stdout out file nil)\n           :err err\n           :exit exit)))\n\n\n(defn check-p5-fixture\n  \"Run P5 `fixture` in temporary directory `dir`: the fixture source plus,\n   for `:request`-bearing fixtures, the [[p5-prologue]] as\n   `auto_prepend_file`. Returns a check record like [[check-fixture]].\"\n  [dir {:keys [id source request out diag uncaught status oracle]}]\n  (let [file (str (name id) \".php\")\n        pre (str (name id) \"-pre.php\")]\n    (write-source! dir file source)\n    (when request (write-source! dir pre (p5-prologue request)))\n    (let [actual (if request\n                   (run-php-file-with-prepend dir file pre)\n                   (run-php-file dir file))\n          expected-out (or out \"\")\n          expected-diag (vec (or diag []))\n          pass? (and (not= :pending oracle)\n                     (= expected-out (:out actual))\n                     (diag-match? expected-diag (:diag actual))\n                     (= uncaught (:uncaught actual))\n                     (or (nil? status) (= status (:exit actual))))]\n      {:id id,\n       :pass? pass?,\n       :oracle oracle,\n       :expected {:out expected-out, :diag expected-diag, :uncaught uncaught, :status status},\n       :actual (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught]) :exit (:exit actual))})))\n\n\n(defn run-p5\n  \"Run all `p5/fixtures` (the request-context fixtures) against\n   `php:8.3-cli`.\"\n  []\n  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \"yang-php-oracle-p5-\"\n                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\n    (try\n      (mapv #(check-p5-fixture dir %) p5/fixtures)\n      (finally\n        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\n          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\n\n\n(defn check-p5b2-fixture\n  \"Run P5b2 `fixture` in temporary directory `dir`: the fixture source plus\n   the [[p5b2-prologue]] as `auto_prepend_file` (the ruled recursive merge\n   and, for `:http-profile` fixtures, the explicit initial status 200 — bare\n   CLI starts without the engine's assumed HTTP 200). Returns a check record\n   like [[check-fixture]], with the engine's guest-fatal representation\n   (`:fatal`) compared against the parser's preserved `:fatal`.\"\n  [dir {:keys [id source out diag uncaught status fatal oracle]}]\n  (let [file (str (name id) \".php\")\n        pre (str (name id) \"-pre.php\")\n        fixture (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) p5b2/fixtures))]\n    (write-source! dir file source)\n    (write-source! dir pre (p5b2-prologue fixture))\n    (let [actual (run-php-file-with-prepend dir file pre)\n          expected-out (or out \"\")\n          expected-diag (vec (or diag []))\n          pass? (and (not= :pending oracle)\n                     (= expected-out (:out actual))\n                     (diag-match? expected-diag (:diag actual))\n                     (= uncaught (:uncaught actual))\n                     (= fatal (:fatal actual))\n                     (or (nil? status) (= status (:exit actual))))]\n      {:id id,\n       :pass? pass?,\n       :oracle oracle,\n       :expected {:out expected-out, :diag expected-diag, :uncaught uncaught,\n                  :fatal fatal, :status status},\n       :actual (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught :fatal]) :exit (:exit actual))})))\n\n\n(defn run-p5b2\n  \"Run all `p5b2/fixtures` (the B2 step-7 fixtures) against `php:8.3-cli`.\"\n  []\n  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \"yang-php-oracle-p5b2-\"\n                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\n    (try\n      (mapv #(check-p5b2-fixture dir %) p5b2/fixtures)\n      (finally\n        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\n          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\n\n\n(defn print-fold\n  \"Print the fold lines for `results`: one paste-ready record per fixture\n   in the P4 [[p4/pin]] shape `{:oracle p5-banner :out :diag :uncaught}`,\n   carrying the guest-fatal representation (`:fatal`) and the process exit\n   status (`:status`) alongside.\"\n  [results]\n  (doseq [{:keys [id actual]} results]\n    (println \"FOLD\" (name id)\n             (pr-str (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught :fatal])\n                            :oracle p5-banner\n                            :status (:exit actual))))))\n\n\n(defn run-all\n  \"Run all `programs/fixtures`, `matrix-source` and `float-cases` against\n   `php:8.3-cli`.\"\n  []\n  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \"yang-php-oracle-\"\n                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\n    (try\n      (-> (mapv #(check-fixture dir %) (concat programs/fixtures p3b/all-fixtures p4/all-fixtures p6/all-fixtures))\n          (conj (check-matrix dir))\n          (conj (check-floats dir)))\n      (finally\n        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\n          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& args]\n  (when (some #{\"--print-prologue\"} args)\n    (let [id (keyword (or (second (drop-while #(not= \"--print-prologue\" %) args))\n                          \"superglobals-from-request\"))\n          fixture (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) p5/fixtures))\n          b2-fixture (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) p5b2/fixtures))]\n      (when-not (or fixture b2-fixture)\n        (println \"Unknown P5 fixture:\" id)\n        (System/exit 2))\n      ;; Dry run: no docker, no oracle. Print the generated prologue for\n      ;; eyeball comparison against the engine's expected superglobal\n      ;; values (the fixture's hand-derived :out is the reference).\n      (print (if b2-fixture\n               (p5b2-prologue b2-fixture)\n               (p5-prologue (:request fixture))))\n      (flush)\n      (shutdown-agents)\n      (System/exit 0)))\n  (when (some #{\"--p5\"} args)\n    (let [results (run-p5)\n          recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\n          failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\n      (println \"Banner:\" p5-banner)\n      (println \"Checked:\" (count results) \"P5 targets; failures:\" (count failures))\n      (print-fold recorded)\n      (doseq [f failures]\n        (println \"FAIL\" (:id f))\n        (println \"  expected:\" (pr-str (:expected f)))\n        (println \"  actual:  \" (pr-str (:actual f))))\n      (shutdown-agents)\n      (when (seq failures)\n        (System/exit 1))\n      (System/exit 0)))\n  (when (some #{\"--p5b2\"} args)\n    (let [results (run-p5b2)\n          recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\n          failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\n      (println \"Banner:\" p5-banner)\n      (println \"Checked:\" (count results) \"P5b2 targets; failures:\" (count failures))\n      (print-fold recorded)\n      (doseq [f failures]\n        (println \"FAIL\" (:id f))\n        (println \"  expected:\" (pr-str (:expected f)))\n        (println \"  actual:  \" (pr-str (:actual f))))\n      (shutdown-agents)\n      (when (seq failures)\n        (System/exit 1))\n      (System/exit 0)))\n  (let [results (run-all)\n        recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\n        failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\n(ns yang.php.antlr.generators-test\n  \"P4 S8 generators, live iteration and protocol integration on the JVM.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as h]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p4 :as p4]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n    [yin.vm.values :as values])\n  (:import\n    [java.util IdentityHashMap]))\n\n\n(def ^:private vms [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n\n\n(deftest generator-fixtures-on-every-vm-test\n  (doseq [{:keys [id source out]} p4/generators-v1]\n    (testing (name id)\n      (let [results (h/run-php source)]\n        (is (not (contains? results :diagnostics)) (pr-str results))\n        (doseq [k vms]\n          (is (= out (get results k)) (str (name id) \" on \" k)))))))\n\n\n(deftest iteration-protocols-test\n  (testing \"Iterator drives foreach directly\"\n    (is (= \"01\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\n                            \"<?php class I implements Iterator { private $i=0; function rewind(): void {$this->i=0;} function valid(): bool {return $this->i<2;} function current(): mixed {return $this->i;} function key(): mixed {return $this->i;} function next(): void {$this->i++;} } foreach(new I as $v) echo $v;\")))))\n  (testing \"IteratorAggregate supplies the live iterator\"\n    (is (= \"23\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\n                            \"<?php class I implements Iterator {private $i=2;function rewind():void{}function valid():bool{return $this->i<4;}function current(){return $this->i;}function key(){return $this->i;}function next():void{$this->i++;}} class A implements IteratorAggregate {function getIterator():Iterator{return new I;}} foreach(new A as $v)echo $v;\")))))\n  (testing \"property iteration filters visibility from the calling scope\"\n    (is (= \"aabc\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\n                              \"<?php class P {public $a='a'; protected $b='b'; private $c='c'; function f(){foreach($this as $v)echo $v;}} $p=new P;foreach($p as $v)echo $v;$p->f();\")))))\n  (testing \"ArrayAccess reads by value; Countable and Stringable dispatch\"\n    (is (= \"43s\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\n                             \"<?php class A implements ArrayAccess, Countable, Stringable {function offsetExists($x):bool{return true;} function offsetGet($x){return 4;} function offsetSet($x,$v):void{} function offsetUnset($x):void{} function count():int{return 3;} function __toString():string{return 's';}} $a=new A;echo $a[0],count($a),(string)$a;\"))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private opts\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n   :capability-secret tu/secret\n   :primitives vm/primitives\n   :modules (h/host-registry)})\n\n\n(def ^:private load-semantic\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\n---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \"Remote test servers\" below for\n# which lanes may overlap.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\n# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\n# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\n# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\n# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs once daily on the remote hosts (04:00 VN);\n# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01;\n# for a fix branch, the previously-failing tests green IS the merge bar\n# (owner ruling 2026-11-07; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n```\n\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
